The latest MSTest is **v4.2.3** (a major version bump from your 3.8.0). Here are the breaking changes relevant to your project:

---

## 1. `[ExpectedException]` is removed ❌

Your tests use `[ExpectedException(...)]` which no longer exists in v4. Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>()`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

## 2. `Assert.IsTrue(true)` triggers warning MSTEST0032

Your `Validate_ValidInput_Succeeds` test has `Assert.IsTrue(true)` — this now emits a **warning** (promoted from Info). Replace with a meaningful assertion or remove it.

## 3. Other notable v4 breaking changes (not directly hitting your code, but good to know):

| Change | Impact |
|--------|--------|
| `TestMethodAttribute.Execute` → `ExecuteAsync` | Only if you have custom test method attributes |
| `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed | Only if you specified `EndOfClass` explicitly |
| `TestContext.Properties` is now `IDictionary<string, object>` | If you use `.Contains()` → use `.ContainsKey()` |
| `Assert` APIs no longer accept `message` + `params object[]` | Use string interpolation instead |
| Minimum TFM is .NET 8+ | You're on net8.0, so you're fine |
| `TestTimeout.Infinite` removed | Use `int.MaxValue` directly |

---

## To upgrade

Update your `.csproj`:
```xml
<PackageReference Include="MSTest" Version="4.2.3" />
```

And fix your test file like this:

```csharp
using Microsoft.VisualStudio.TestTools.UnitTesting;

namespace MyApp.Tests;

[TestClass]
public class ValidationServiceTests
{
    [TestMethod]
    public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
    {
        Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void Process_InvalidState_ThrowsInvalidOperation()
    {
        Assert.ThrowsExactly<InvalidOperationException>(() => Process());
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void Validate_ValidInput_Succeeds()
    {
        // Replace with a meaningful assertion
        Assert.IsTrue(true);
    }
    // ...
}
```

Would you like me to apply these changes to your project?
